{"name":"Snow Peak","hex":"#e0dcdb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The partly frozen, crystalline state of water that falls from the atmosphere as precipitation in flakes; also, the falling of such flakes; and the accumulation of them on the ground or on objects as a white layer.\n\n An instance of the falling of snow (etymology 1, noun sense 1); a snowfall; also, a snowstorm.","An instance of the falling of snow (etymology 1, noun sense 1); a snowfall; also, a snowstorm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Preceded by the dummy subject it: to have snow (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1) fall from the atmosphere.","Of a thing: to fall like snow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snow"},{"term":"peak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A point; the sharp end or top of anything that terminates in a point; as, the peak, or front, of a cap.","The highest value reached by some quantity in a time period."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To raise the point of (a gaff) closer to perpendicular.","To raise an oar out of the water, fitting the handle into a round slot or socket located at the bottom of the boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Piton des Neiges","blocks":[{"text":"The Piton des Neiges is a 3,069 m (10,069 ft) complex volcano on Réunion, one of the French volcanic islands in the Mascarene Archipelago in the southwestern Indian Ocean. It is located about 800 kilometres (500 mi) east of Madagascar. Piton des Neiges is the highest point on Réunion and considered to be the highest point in the Indian Ocean. Piton des Neiges is ranked 82nd by prominence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/PitonDesNeiges.JPG/330px-PitonDesNeiges.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piton_des_Neiges"},{"title":"Snow Peak (Alberta)","blocks":[{"text":"Snow Peak is a 2,789-metre (9,150-foot) mountain summit in the Spray Mountains, a sub-range of the Canadian Rockies in Alberta, Canada. The mountain is situated on the shared border of Peter Lougheed Provincial Park and Banff National Park. The nearest higher peak is Mount Birdwood, 1.64 km (1.02 mi) to the northeast. The mountain is primarily used for hiking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Snow_Peak%2C_Spray_Mountains.jpg/330px-Snow_Peak%2C_Spray_Mountains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_Peak_(Alberta)"},{"title":"Snow Peak (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Snow Peak, Inc.  is a Japanese manufacturer of high-end camping and hiking equipment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Snow_Peak_Headquarters_Niigata_Sanjo_Shitada_May2023.jpg/330px-Snow_Peak_Headquarters_Niigata_Sanjo_Shitada_May2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_Peak_(company)"},{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/P%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg/500px-P%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/P%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg/1280px-P%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/P%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg/500px-P%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AP%C3%AEton_des_Neiges_Panorama.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Reunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg/500px-Reunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Reunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg/1280px-Reunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Reunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg/500px-Reunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The island of Reunion with the three central Cirques, with the ridge summit of the Piton des Neiges in the northwest centre (lighter brown area). The white spot on the crater edge to the southeast of the summit is the alpine hut.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReunion_21.12S_55.51E.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Sunrise_from_Piton_Des_Neiges.jpg/500px-Sunrise_from_Piton_Des_Neiges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Sunrise_from_Piton_Des_Neiges.jpg/1280px-Sunrise_from_Piton_Des_Neiges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x